 tags</b> (<code>text-cyan-300 bg-cyan-500/15</code>). \"\n            \"<br/>• Complexity expressions <code>$O(N)$</code> are styled with <b>Emerald mathematical badges</b>. \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>### Approach</code> headers are converted to clean visual section cards (Red for Brute Force, Yellow for Better, Green for Optimal).\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q9. Database Design: What is your database schema and indexing strategy?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: The database schema is organized across key relational entities: \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>users</code> (id, username, email, password_hash, rating, wins, losses, win_streak, global_rank). \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>problems</code> (id, title, slug [INDEX], difficulty [INDEX], topics [INDEX], patterns, starter_codes, editorial). \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>test_cases</code> (id, problem_id [FOREIGN KEY], input_data, expected_output, is_hidden, order_index). \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>matches</code> & <code>submissions</code> (match_id, player_id, problem_id, verdict, runtime_ms, memory_mb, efficiency_score). \"\n            \"<br/>Indexes on <code>slug</code>, <code>difficulty</code>, <code>topics</code>, and <code>rating DESC</code> ensure sub-millisecond leaderboard queries.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q10. Scalability & System Design: How would you scale CodeDuel to 100,000 concurrent active users?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: \"\n            \"<br/>1. <b>Decoupled Asynchronous Judge Workers</b>: Extract code execution out of web nodes into a distributed queue (e.g. RabbitMQ or Apache Kafka). Ephemeral Docker containers/Firecracker microVMs scale horizontally on Kubernetes (K8s) to consume judge tasks. \"\n            \"<br/>2. <b>Distributed WebSocket Relays</b>: Use Redis Pub/Sub as the STOMP message broker relay across multiple Spring Boot web nodes behind an Nginx/ALB load balancer. \"\n            \"<br/>3. <b>Database Read Replicas & Redis Caching</b>: Route read-heavy leaderboard and problem catalog queries to read replicas while caching the Top 1,000 players in Redis Sorted Sets (<code>ZREVRANGE</code> in O(log N + M)).\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q11. Testing & Verification: How did you ensure 100% data integrity across all 1,000 questions?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: We wrote an automated Spring Boot integration test (<code>All1000ProblemsVerificationTest.java</code>) that validates: \"\n            \"<br/>• Exactly 1,000 questions seeded across 16 DSA categories with zero null or empty fields. \"\n            \"<br/>• Exactly 5,000 test cases (5 per problem) strictly matching input/output types (e.g. booleans produce 'true'/'false'). \"\n            \"<br/>• Every editorial contains the complete 3-Tier Approach structure (Brute Force, Better, Most Optimal, and Interview Pitfalls). \"\n            \"<br/>• 12/12 test suites execute and pass with <code>BUILD SUCCESS</code>.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q12. Behavioral: What was the most challenging technical hurdle you solved on this project?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: <i>'The most challenging problem was designing a generic, high-speed execution sandbox capable of testing arbitrary Java and Python code with heterogeneous method signatures without manual per-problem compilation scripts. Initially, signature mismatches caused compilation errors when users switched problems. I resolved this by designing a unified 9-archetype signature classification system combined with runtime reflection in Java and dynamic signature introspection in Python. This reduced execution overhead to under 100ms per test case and guaranteed 100% test case compatibility across all 1,000 questions.'</i>\"\n        )\n    ]\n    \n    for q_title, ans_text in qa_list:\n        qa_card_data = [\n            [Paragraph(q_title, q_style)],\n            [HRFlowable(width=\"100%\", thickness=0.5, color=colors.HexColor(\"#e2e8f0\"), spaceBefore=2, spaceAfter=4)],\n            [Paragraph(ans_text, ans_style)]\n        ]\n        qa_card = Table(qa_card_data, colWidths=[504])\n        qa_card.setStyle(TableStyle([\n            ('BACKGROUND', (0,0), (-1,-1), colors.HexColor(\"#ffffff\")),\n            ('BOX', (0,0), (-1,-1), 0.75, colors.HexColor(\"#e2e8f0\")),\n            ('TOPPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 6),\n            ('BOTTOMPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 6),\n            ('LEFTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 10),\n            ('RIGHTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 10),\n            ('VALIGN', (0,0), (-1,-1), 'TOP'),\n        ]))\n        story.append(qa_card)\n        story.append(Spacer(1, 8))\n        \n    doc.build(story, canvasmaker=NumberedCanvas)\n    print(f\"PDF generated successfully at: {pdf_path}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    generate_pdf()\n","Description":"Python script to generate professional CodeDuel Interview Preparation Guide PDF","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\codeduel\\generate_interview_pdf.py","toolAction":"Writing PDF generator script","toolSummary":"Create PDF generator script"}}]}
